BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Wallace & Gromit: The Classic Shorts (4K Restorations!)
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20270109T160000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20270109T174500
DTSTAMP:20270110T000000Z
UID:wallace-gromit-the-classic-shorts-4k-restorations-2027-01-09-16:00:00-
 08:00
DESCRIPTION:Back on the big screen for the first time in ages! Aardman Ani
 mation’s beloved duo of clueless inventor Wallace and his wise\, world-w
 eary dog companion Gromit first took the world by storm in this trio of sw
 eetly absurd Oscar-winning shorts by visionary animator Nick Park. Full of
  stunning filmmaking and design\, clever writing and deep emotional beats
 \, this timeless program of claymation is for the kid in us all.\n\nA GRAN
 D DAY OUT (1989\, 25 mins.)\nTalented but unlucky inventor Wallace travels
  with his loyal sidekick on a cheese-seeking moon quest.\n\nTHE WRONG TROU
 SERS (1993\, 30 mins.)\nWallace’s latest invention – a pair of “Tech
 no Trousers” – leads to danger from penguin supervillain Feathers McGr
 aw.\n\nA CLOSE SHAVE (1995\, 30 mins.)\nWallace has a new invention – a 
 Knit-O-Matic machine – and adventure looms as sheep are being rustled an
 d poor Gromit is framed. Keep your eyes peeled for Shaun the Sheep in his 
 big-screen debut!\n\nNick Park\, United Kingdom\, 1989-1995\, 85 min\, in 
 English\n\nhttps://nwfilmforum.org/films/wallace-gromit-the-classic-shorts
 -4k-restorations/\n\nEstimated start: 16:20
LOCATION:Northwest Film Forum\, 1515 12th Ave\, Seattle\, WA 98122
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Xanadu (1980)
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261208T190000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261208T210000
DTSTAMP:20261209T030000Z
UID:xanadu-2026-12-08-19:00:00-08:00
DESCRIPTION:Struggling artist Sonny Malone (Michael Beck) is trapped in a 
 dull job painting album covers. He is instantly attracted to Kira (Olivia 
 Newton-John)\, an anonymous woman randomly photographed in the background 
 of one of his assignments\, but no one is able to identify her. Visiting t
 he auditorium where the cover was shot\, Sonny finds the mysterious beauty
 \, an ageless Greek muse\, who encourages him to team up with old-fashione
 d Danny McGuire (Gene Kelly) to build a roller-skating disco.\n\nRobert Gr
 eenwald\, United States\, 1980\, 96 min\, in English\n\nhttps://nwfilmforu
 m.org/films/xanadu/\n\nEstimated start: 19:20
LOCATION:Northwest Film Forum\, 1515 12th Ave\, Seattle\, WA 98122
END:VEVENT
